                                                                                                                <comments>
                            <comment id="16038026" author="cos" created="Tue, 6 Jun 2017 02:48:05 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Here&apos;s the patch to turn this functionality off completely until the time we know what and how to deal with this.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16038041" author="cos" created="Tue, 6 Jun 2017 03:14:01 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Even more explicit version of the patch.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16039335" author="dmagda" created="Tue, 6 Jun 2017 17:50:09 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=cos&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;cos&quot;&gt;cos&lt;/a&gt;, looks good to me. Please merge to the master. The next release will be synced up with the master.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16039372" author="cos" created="Tue, 6 Jun 2017 18:08:05 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;The fix  is committed to the master as c3b8998.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16047622" author="gstein" created="Tue, 13 Jun 2017 09:08:18 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Note: the ASF now owns the &quot;ignite.run&quot; domain and does not specify any &quot;A&quot; records for it. Thus, old/current versions will be unable to contact any third-party systems.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Caveat: cached A records&lt;br/&gt;
Caveat: very early systems that used http: and subject to MITM attacks&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
